455
00:38:49,060 --> 00:38:50,540
Then the street is closed.

456
00:38:51,500 --> 00:38:53,200
The easy part is the actual towing.

457
00:38:56,000 --> 00:39:01,080
The hard part is getting around all the obstructions, like electrical and telephone wires.

458
00:39:01,720 --> 00:39:09,300
The cost of getting overhead wires raised was greater than the cost of taking the roof off of the building and putting it back on.

459
00:39:09,800 --> 00:39:15,520
So the customer decided to take the roof off as opposed to getting the wires raised.

460
00:39:15,521 --> 00:39:22,520
As Ted Hollinger struggles to move heaven and earth with his church moving project,

461
00:39:22,521 --> 00:39:26,420
a private company is using towing in an effort to move

462
00:39:26,421 --> 00:39:30,840
from earth to the heavens. Welcome to the Eclipse program.

463
00:39:30,841 --> 00:39:37,640
The Eclipse program is a reusable launch vehicle development program that basically employs

464
00:39:37,641 --> 00:39:42,360
towing as a key technology and that basically

465
00:39:42,361 --> 00:39:47,860
toes behind the four-engine transport jet, the rocket-powered glider aircraft.

466
00:39:47,861 --> 00:39:53,320
And we do this basically to use the tow airplane as a first stage.

467
00:39:54,740 --> 00:40:00,040
The second stage is launching that rocket into space from an altitude of about 20,000 feet.

468
00:40:01,640 --> 00:40:03,620
And why would anyone want to do that?

469
00:40:04,300 --> 00:40:08,180
You can basically launch from virtually any place on the globe,

470
00:40:08,181 --> 00:40:14,240
and so you don't need to have a whole series of facility infrastructure and everything to support this,

471
00:40:14,241 --> 00:40:18,540
which is very, very expensive and adds to the cost of launches.

472
00:40:20,160 --> 00:40:26,620
Further, launching after being towed to 20,000 feet avoids putting your craft through the enormous physical stress

473
00:40:26,621 --> 00:40:29,320
and expensive extra fuel of a vertical takeoff,

474
00:40:29,760 --> 00:40:33,800
where much of your energy is spent in those first violent seconds.

475
00:40:33,801 --> 00:40:42,420
In fact, a towed launch can save between 10 and 25% of the total energy used in a conventional

476
00:40:42,421 --> 00:40:44,420
vertical launch.

477
00:40:44,421 --> 00:40:51,340
Plus, you're that much closer to your destination when you're already up in the air.

478
00:40:51,341 --> 00:40:56,000
It's also more pleasant for a passenger to jet into space airplane-like than to rocket

479
00:40:56,001 --> 00:40:58,520
into space ballistic missile-like.

480
00:40:58,521 --> 00:41:03,480
Because Mike Gallo doesn't want to send astronauts into space, he wants to send you there.

481
00:41:03,481 --> 00:41:10,480
Once you enable the masses to experience space and participate,

482
00:41:10,481 --> 00:41:14,480
and you can deliver them to and from space economically,

483
00:41:14,481 --> 00:41:18,480
cost-effectively, of course, reliably, and routinely,

484
00:41:18,481 --> 00:41:22,480
those are key criteria towards enabling the growth of space.

485
00:41:22,481 --> 00:41:24,480
That's right.

486
00:41:24,481 --> 00:41:28,480
For a one-hour flight that includes a 15- to 30-minute interlude

487
00:41:28,481 --> 00:41:31,480
into the realm of astronauts, of weightlessness,

488
00:41:31,481 --> 00:41:33,800
60 and 100 miles above the Earth,

489
00:41:34,500 --> 00:41:37,000
the eclipse can take you to Kathmandu,

490
00:41:37,620 --> 00:41:40,060
or Moscow, or Hong Kong,

491
00:41:40,940 --> 00:41:44,320
or for a slightly longer flight, perhaps, the moon.

492
00:41:46,420 --> 00:41:49,440
He says he needs just another 5 to 10 years.

493
00:41:50,040 --> 00:41:53,540
We spent a couple of years looking at the dynamics

494
00:41:53,541 --> 00:41:56,860
and the behavioral characteristics of towing and the tow line

495
00:41:56,861 --> 00:41:59,300
and the bungee effect, we call it, you know,

496
00:41:59,301 --> 00:42:05,980
the oscillations of two aircraft operating in close proximity to each other and actually

497
00:42:05,981 --> 00:42:10,060
imposes some substantial loads.

498
00:42:10,061 --> 00:42:15,780
The Eclipse project will eventually use a 747 passenger plane as its tower, which is

499
00:42:15,781 --> 00:42:22,680
normally capable of towing a vehicle with an 850,000 pound takeoff weight.

500
00:42:22,681 --> 00:42:28,300
The 1 1⁄2 inch fiber tow rope weighs several thousand pounds itself and is about a thousand

501
00:42:28,301 --> 00:42:31,694
feet long, but can pay out to over 5,000 feet.

502
00:42:31,695 --> 00:42:34,940
Eclipse scientists had to work within what's

503
00:42:34,941 --> 00:42:41,020
called a low-tow configuration, in which the tow vehicle takes off first, levels at about 200 feet,

504
00:42:41,580 --> 00:42:47,100
then the vehicle being towed takes off and stays below the first plane's wash, or turbulent airflow.

505
00:42:49,020 --> 00:42:52,540
The Eclipse scientists have discovered something else during their rocket tests.

506
00:42:54,300 --> 00:42:57,340
It's something that seems universal across the panoply of towing.

507
00:42:58,300 --> 00:43:02,860
Something Ernest Holmes might have told them from the front seat of his cobbled tow truck in Chattanooga.

508
00:43:04,800 --> 00:43:10,140
While the dynamics and the mathematics and the prediction models are very complex,

509
00:43:10,560 --> 00:43:15,180
what we really found out is the simplicity of how it works.

510
00:43:17,580 --> 00:43:23,500
Towing really is just a hook and a chain, a winch and an engine, a tug and a pull.

511
00:43:24,800 --> 00:43:27,860
Towing seems simple when cars are being pulled out of ditches.

512
00:43:28,300 --> 00:43:35,300
Less so when railroads are hauling passengers up mountains or airplanes are hoisting rockets into space.

513
00:43:35,301 --> 00:43:43,300
So when the New Hampshire legislature joked in 1858 that Sylvester Marsh ought to build his cog railway to the moon,

514
00:43:43,301 --> 00:43:48,300
they had no idea Mike Gallo would someday take them up on it.

